== the sea walls on the east coast
tier: decision
cast_want: decide
sphere: prot
scope: nation
stages: adult mature elder
age: 30-90
tone: trouble
life: home, community
horizon: years
roles: colleague, rival, elder
earth: the sea walls along the coast are old and the money will mend half of them, and {N} decides which
scene: The sea walls along the east coast were built by the grandparents of the people behind them, and the last storm opened three of them. The money in the budget will mend half the walls at most. The coastal towns, the farmers on the low fields and the engineers all have a plan, and the choice is {Ns}.
- U | mend the walls the flood models say protect the most homes | v: achievement, security | scope: nation | lever: lead | chance: 60
- G | let the lowest fields go back to salt marsh, which holds the sea better than walls | v: universalism, security | scope: nation | lever: found | chance: 55
- W | mend every wall a little, so that no stretch of coast is left out | v: universalism, conformity | scope: nation | lever: loyalty | chance: 55
- B | mend first the walls of the towns that pay half the cost | v: power, security | scope: nation | lever: fund | chance: 60
works: The next winter's storms come and go, and the walls and the marsh both hold.
works: {elder}, who has farmed the low fields all a long life, says the plan was hard but right.
fails: A stretch of coast left for later floods in the spring, and the families there want to know why.
fails: {rival} says the plan picked winners and losers along the coast, and the losers agree.

== the country's emergency lines
tier: decision
cast_want: decide
sphere: prot
scope: nation
stages: adult mature elder
age: 30-90
tone: mixed
life: health, community
horizon: years
roles: colleague, rival
earth: the emergency lines are answered by forty local rooms of mixed quality, and their future is {Ns} to decide
scene: The country's emergency calls are answered by forty local rooms. Some answer in seconds and some in minutes, and the rooms in the hills are the slowest. The review of how the calls are answered, and who is sent, has come to {N}.
- U | merge the rooms into a few large ones, run by the figures | v: achievement, security | scope: nation | lever: lead | chance: 60
- G | keep the local rooms, where the call takers know every lane | v: tradition, security | scope: nation | lever: loyalty | chance: 60
- R | start sending trained volunteers by phone alert in three regions before the assembly votes | v: stimulation, benevolence | scope: nation | lever: subvert | chance: 55
- W | one standard every room must meet, with the same answer time across the country | v: universalism, conformity | scope: nation | lever: lead | chance: 60
works: A year on, the calls are answered faster in most of the country, and the hill rooms have caught up.
works: {colleague} says the crews say help is reaching people sooner than it used to.
fails: The change is slow to bed in, and a few bad nights in the first winter make the news.
fails: {rival} says the review was decided before it began, and the rooms' staff say the same.
